FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: eleven-sons.
OFF THE RECORD: Store eleven named values in a register. THE ROSTER OF returns
OFF THE RECORD: the keys in alphabetical order.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT sons IS AN EMPTY REGISTER.
    INSCRIBE "handsome, but a trifle shallow" UNDER "first" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "at home in the world, and it shows" UNDER "second" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "beautiful, and not to my taste" UNDER "third" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "open-hearted; one worries" UNDER "fourth" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "kind, and impossible to praise" UNDER "fifth" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "thoughtful, or at least stooped" UNDER "sixth" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "witty in a way the age rejects" UNDER "seventh" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "my child of sorrow, who keeps his distance" UNDER "eighth" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "elegant, with the wrong friends" UNDER "ninth" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "so earnest he is suspected of irony" UNDER "tenth" IN sons.
    INSCRIBE "delicate, but the delicacy is a kind of strength" UNDER "eleventh" IN sons.
    PROCLAIM "I have " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF THE LENGTH OF sons PLUS " sons.".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT roll IS THE ROSTER OF sons.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT i IS 0.

ARTICLE 2.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT i IS i PLUS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT son IS THE ITEM AT i IN roll.
    PROCLAIM "the " PLUS son PLUS ": " PLUS THE ENTRY UNDER son IN sons.
    SHOULD i FALL SHORT OF THE LENGTH OF sons, REFER TO ARTICLE 2.

ARTICLE 3.
    PROCLAIM "These are my eleven sons. The Court has filed them in its own order; so, I suppose, have I.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
